Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodologies

Part 6 — Unity Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodology (Beginner → Expert)

> Goal: Learn how to systematically understand Android applications built with the Unity engine. Unity applications differ significantly from conventional Android apps because the Android layer mainly boots the Unity runtime, while the majority of application logic executes inside the Unity engine. By the end of this section, you should be able to reconstruct scene architecture, object hierarchies, gameplay systems, rendering, physics, asset organization, scripting, and the interaction between Unity and Android.



> Core Principle:
Reverse engineer the Unity engine's execution model first, then recover the game's systems, architecture, and content built on top of it.




