Stage 30 — Common Unity Investigation Mistakes

Avoid

Treating Unity like a standard Android application.

Spending excessive time in the Android bootstrap instead of the Unity runtime.

Confusing engine components with gameplay systems.

Ignoring scene boundaries.

Following individual GameObjects before understanding subsystems.

Mixing engine lifecycle with gameplay lifecycle.

Assuming every native library contains game logic.



---

Stage 31 — Unity APK Methodology Master Checklist

By the end of this stage, you should be able to:

✅ Identify Unity applications and determine the scripting backend.

✅ Reconstruct scene hierarchies, GameObjects, Components, and gameplay systems.

✅ Understand Unity's execution order, rendering, animation, physics, and resource loading.

✅ Recover persistence, networking, UI architecture, and plugin integration.

✅ Trace communication between Unity, native Android code, and platform services.

✅ Distinguish Unity engine infrastructure from handwritten game logic.

✅ Validate reconstructed architecture using runtime behavior.

✅ Produce comprehensive documentation describing the Unity application's architecture, execution model, and gameplay systems.



